<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John the Fearless</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1371–1419</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as John I, Duke of Burgundy, John the Fearless of Burgundy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John the Fearless was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> from 1404 until 1419, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-bold">Philip the Bold</a>. Captured at Nicopolis in 1396 and victor over Liège at Othée in 1408, he had <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-duke-of-orleans">Louis of Orléans</a> murdered in 1407, which began the civil war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundians">Burgundians</a> and Armagnacs. He was himself murdered on the bridge at Montereau in 1419 by followers of the Dauphin, which drove his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a> into alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-the-fearless.jpg" alt="John the Fearless" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous / After Jean Malouel / School of Jan van Eyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_II,_Duke_of_Burgundy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
